  "description": "BAGVOX crystallizes in the monoclinic crystal system with space group P 21/c. Reported CIF formula moiety: C80 H102 Gd4 N8 Ni3 O41,C4 H10 O1,1.5(C1 H4 O1),1.75(H2 O1). From the CIF bond table, Gd1 (Gd) has 9 O neighbors; Gd2 (Gd) has 8 O neighbors; Gd3 (Gd) has 8 O neighbors; Gd4 (Gd) has 8 O neighbors; Ni1 (Ni) has 4 O neighbors; Ni2 (Ni) has 4 O neighbors; Ni3 (Ni) has 4 O neighbors. Oxygen-bridged metal-site graph: 9 pairs, 2 components; largest component is a network with cycles with approximately planar metal-site arrangement. Computed bridged metal-metal separations span 3.224-4.336 Å (not direct metal-metal bonds). Computed M-O-M angles span 87.11-133.09°; individual values and O labels are in metal_framework.links. Article card reports molecular formula C80H102Gd4N8Ni3O41·Et2O·1.5MeOH·1.75H2O. Explicit grouped units in the article formula/name: 6 OAc (explicit grouped unit in article compound name (structural notation)), 3 NO3 (explicit grouped unit in article compound name (structural notation)), 3 OH (explicit grouped unit in article compound name (structural notation)).",
